# Slice 2.5 Risks

Threat-model for the side-car shell. **Slice 2.5 is additive dark-launch** — the side-car is shadow infra (spawned, supervised, listening) with nothing depending on it.

Risks #2, #5, #8 are **structurally eliminated** by this posture and are omitted from the table below — see "Why dark-launch collapses the risk surface". They return at the renderer cutover (slice 2.6); mitigate them there. Risk numbers are kept stable (gaps intentional) so cross-references to the plan stay valid.

**All remaining risks are Low** — every Blocker / High / Medium has been designed down. Each has a named, structural fix baked into the slice.

